      "audio": {
        "id": 16,
        "title": "Want a better winter workout? Train your muscle clocks",
        "source": "NPR Short Wave",
        "source_id": "npr_short_wave",
        "category": "culture",
        "url": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/25/nx-s1-6034942/winter-exercise-circadian-rhythm-arc",
        "published_at": "2026-11-25T08:00:00",
        "level": "B2",
        "slot_level": "B2",
        "source_level": "B2",
        "word_count": 138,
        "duration_sec": 801,
        "body_text": null,
        "audio_url": "https://npr.simplecastaudio.com/72da6803-9aa4-4e2e-a973-3bc436f0e9fa/episodes/3350ed11-22b2-4401-8522-2fb82131112d/audio/128/default.mp3/default.mp3_ywr3ahjkcgo_b18837de46bac7db2bb26a398f717d2c_15683531.mp3?awCollectionId=72da6803-9aa4-4e2e-a973-3bc436f0e9fa&awEpisodeId=3350ed11-22b2-4401-8522-2fb82131112d&feed=F0qJcgXZ&t=podcast&e=nx-s1-6034942&p=510351&d=801&size=12824703&hash_redirect=1&x-total-bytes=15683531&x-ais-classified=unclassified&x-access-range=0-1023&listeningSessionID=0CD_382_328__fe93f1882f6e1e609902b22888e7e4b88d6a8eea",
        "description": "TikTok has another trend: the winter arc. It’s a self-improvement challenge where people try to be their best self in the 3 months leading up to New Year – often, through exercise. We at Short Wave wanted to know if the science really holds up: Is ramping up your exercise routine when your circadian rhythm may be struggling with less light really a good idea? So we called up NPR health correspondent, Will Stone . He’s done a deep dive on what scientists do and don’t know about exercise and our circadian rhythms. To read more of Will’s reporting on creating a solid exercise routine . If you liked this episode, check out our episodes on “circadian depression” , and the science of jet lag and how to avoid it. Interested in more health science? Email us your question at shortwave@npr.org .",
        "license": "proprietary",
        "attribution": null,
        "truncated": false,
        "guid_hash": "585facf6bbdf012ca999de74fc617b26a04cc8ba",
        "summary": "TikTok has another trend: the winter arc. It’s a self-improvement challenge where people try to be their best self in the 3 months leading up to New Year – often, through exercise. We at Short Wave wanted to know if the science really holds up: Is ramping up your exercise routine when your circadian rhythm may be struggling with less light really a good idea? So we called up NPR health correspondent, Will Stone . He’s done a deep dive on what scientists do and don’t know about exercise and our circadian rhythms. To read more of Will’s reporting on creating a solid exercise routine . If you liked this episode, check out our episodes on “circadian depression” , and the science of jet lag and how to avoid it. Interested in more health science? Email us your question at shortwave@npr.org .",
